{"term":"forgive","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e7b1d6d292dd38696c","definition":"To pardon (someone); to waive any negative feeling towards or desire for punishment or retribution against.","example":"Please forgive me if my phone goes off - I'm expecting an urgent call from my boss.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["forgivability","forgivable","forgive and forget","forgive but don't forget","forgiveless","forgive my French","forgiveness","forgiver","forgiving","misforgive","reforgive","unforgive","unforgiver"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forgive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:836114eed532b64963","definition":"To pardon (something); to waive any negative feeling over or retribution for.","example":"Forgive these wild and wandering cries,\n⁠Confusions of a wasted youth;\n⁠Forgive them where they fail in truth,\nAnd in thy wisdom make me wise.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["forgivability","forgivable","forgive and forget","forgive but don't forget","forgiveless","forgive my French","forgiveness","forgiver","forgiving","misforgive","reforgive","unforgive","unforgiver"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/forgive#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d1a72f4b80c796d8ea","definition":"To waive or remit (a debt), to absolve from payment or compensation of.","example":"Forgive a debt, that is, tell a debtor that a repayment of a loan is no longer needed.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["forgivability","forgivable","forgive and forget","forgive but don't forget","forgiveless","forgive my French","forgiveness","forgiv